{"id":"n5-066","title":"いくつ～","romaji":"ikutsu~","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"Used to express 'how many' or ask for the number of something.","longExplanation":"The grammar point いくつ is used when asking or expressing 'how many' of something there are, or to indicate an unspecified number. In English, it can be translated as 'how many' or 'several'.","formation":"いくつ + Noun (optional)","examples":[{"jp":"リンゴはいくつありますか？","romaji":"Ringo wa ikutsu arimasu ka?","en":"How many apples are there?","words":[{"surface":"リンゴ","vocabId":"1555480","reading":"りんご"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いくつ","vocabId":"1219960","reading":"いくつ"},{"surface":"あり","vocabId":"1225940","reading":"あり","baseForm":"ある"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"？","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[2]},{"jp":"いくつかの問題を解決しなければなりません。","romaji":"Ikutsu ka no mondai o kaiketsu shinakereba narimasen.","en":"I have to solve several problems.","words":[{"surface":"いくつ","vocabId":"1219960","reading":"いくつ"},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"問題","vocabId":"1536010","reading":"もんだい"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"解決","vocabId":"1198960","reading":"かいけつ"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"なけれ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ない"},{"surface":"ば","vocabId":null},{"surface":"なり","vocabId":"1899440","reading":"なり","baseForm":"なる"},{"surface":"ませ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"ん","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0]},{"jp":"あなたはいくつの言語を話せますか？","romaji":"Anata wa ikutsu no gengo o hanasemasu ka?","en":"How many languages can you speak?","words":[{"surface":"あなた","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いくつ","vocabId":"1219960","reading":"いくつ"},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"言語","vocabId":"1264420","reading":"げんご"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"話せ","vocabId":"1562360","reading":"はなせ